# Ignore everything by default (project folders have their own repos)
*

# Explicitly include workspace-level shared files
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.vscode/
!.vscode/**
!README.md
!_copilot-shared/
!_copilot-shared/**
!powershell/
!powershell/**
!adding-a-new-subworkspace.md
!repair-workspace-copilot.md
!Visual Studio Code.code-workspace
!Changelog.md
!sanity.bat
!sanity_v.bat
!.markdownlint.json
!*.ps1

# Re-ignore the scanner convenience copies synced to the workspace root.
# The canonical, tracked versions live in _copilot-shared/scaffold/; the root
# copies exist only so the parent repo can run sanity.bat and must not be
# double-tracked. The leading "/" anchors to the workspace root, so the
# scaffold/ copies are unaffected. (security_scan.py is already ignored by the
# "*" rule above - there is no "!*.py" whitelist - but it is listed here too so
# the intent is explicit and both scanners are treated identically.)
/security_scan.py
/security_scan.ps1
